{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VmshbtRonkkKTis3zmQuyh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t?? .ard-input/\n2\tinternal/roles:\n3\tconfig.yaml\n4\tcve_docker_integration_test.go\n5\tcve_integration_test.go\n6\tcve_test.go\n7\tdocs_docker_integration_test.go\n8\tdocs_test.go\n9\teng_review_test.go\n10\tengineer_test.go\n11\terrcodes_integration_test.go\n12\terrcodes_test.go\n13\tlead_test.go\n14\tlicense_review_integration_test.go\n15\tlicense_review_test.go\n16\tmissing_tests_test.go\n17\treviewers\n18\troles.go\n19\troles_test.go\n20\tscanner_guard_test.go\n21\tscanners\n22\tsecurity_review_test.go\n23\ttestdata\n24\ttriage\n25\tworker_engineer_test.go\n26\tworkers\n27\t\n28\tinternal/roles/scanners/cve:\n29\tDockerfile\n30\tmerge.jq\n31\tscan\n32\t\n33\tinternal/roles/scanners/docs:\n34\tDockerfile\n35\tdocscan.go\n36\tscan\n37\t\n38\tinternal/roles/scanners/error-codes:\n39\tDockerfile\n40\terrcodes.jq\n41\tscan\n42\t\n43\tinternal/roles/scanners/missing-tests:\n44\tmissingtests.go\n45\t\n46\tinternal/roles/testdata:\n47\tcve\n48\tdocs\n49\tlts\n50\tmissing-tests\n51\t\n52\t**Dependencies.** #23 (the scanner pipeline) is closed, and that is the only hard dependency. Do not wait for #41, #42 or #46: this change touches none of their code. It follows the pattern of #24 (`scanners/cve`): a `scan` script, a jq program, a pinned Dockerfile, golden fixtures and integration tests behind the `integration` build tag. Sibling scanner issues (#47, #49, #50) can copy the same layout, and no shared code is needed now.\n53\t\n54\t### What was checked on main (2026-11-23)\n55\t\n56\t- `ExecEngine.Scan` (internal/scanner/engine_exec.go) runs `<role dir>/scan` with no arguments. The cwd is a **read-only worktree detached at the config SHA**, the role directory (including its `Extra` files) is mounted read-only, and the run has no GitHub token and no model key, but has network egress. Only stdout is decoded, by the strict `scanner.DecodeFindings`. Any non-zero exit discards the run. A role with a `Dockerfile` runs in that image. A deterministic scanner has `TrustedInput`, so it gets no host-mode warning.\n57\t- `config` discovers `scanners/lint` from the presence of an executable `scan`. `Autoclose` defaults to true for a `scan` scanner. Overrides go in `config.yaml`. The proposal's Configuration example already carries `scanners/lint: { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }`.\n58\t- **golangci-lint v2.15.0 behaviour, checked by hand on a scratch module.** Each item below drives a decision.\n59\t  - With the defaults `max-issues-per-linter: 50` and `max-same-issues: 3`, output is truncated, so findings over the caps would vanish and be **autoclosed**. Both must be forced to `0`.\n60\t  - A repo config with `issues.new: true` (or `new-from-rev`, `new-from-merge-base`, `new-from-patch`) makes a clean read-only checkout report **zero issues**. That would autoclose every lint issue. The flags `--new=false --new-from-rev= --new-from-merge-base= --new-from-patch=` override the config (verified).\n61\t  - With `--issues-exit-code=0`, a compile error comes back as an issue with `FromLinter: \"typecheck\"` and exit 0. It must fail the run.\n62\t  - `--path-mode=abs` gives absolute filenames, which makes multi-module path handling simple.\n63\t  - JSON shape: `{\"Issues\":[{\"FromLinter\",\"Text\",\"Severity\",\"SourceLines\":[..],\"Pos\":{\"Filename\",\"Line\",\"Column\"}}],\"Report\":{...}}`.\n64\t- **ard itself today, golangci-lint v2.15.0 defaults** (errcheck, govet, ineffassign, staticcheck, unused): 300 raw issues, 184 distinct after collapsing (see fingerprint). 273 are errcheck (156 of those in `_test.go`), 2 are `staticcheck SA4000` in `internal/servecmd/reaping_test.go` (look like real bugs), and there are 10 `//nolint` directives. ard's own enablement therefore needs a baseline (see Human follow-up).\n65\t\n66\t### Tech lead view\n67\t\n68\t**Architecture fit.** A deterministic scanner fits the existing pipeline and needs **no Go code change in the controller**. All dedupe, grouping, filing, autoclose and suppression stay in `internal/scanner`. The role directory holds:\n69\t\n70\t```\n71\tinternal/roles/scanners/lint/\n72\t  scan          # sh, 0755: runs golangci-lint per Go module, finds //nolint, calls normalize.jq\n73\t  normalize.jq  # pure: golangci-lint JSON + nolint lines + baseline -> findings JSONL (or baseline text)\n74\t  Dockerfile    # pinned golang base (same digest as cve) + golangci-lint built with it + jq\n75\t```\n76\t\n77\tThe `baseline` is **not** shipped in the starter (see open question 1). It is a human-owned file a repo adds next to `scan`. Because it lives under `.ard/scanners/`, it is a protected path and outside every agent's write allowlist. A worker therefore cannot \"fix\" a lint issue by baselining it. That is the main reason to keep it in the role directory and not at the repo root.\n78\t\n79\t**Invariants (CLAUDE.md).**\n80\t- (1)(2) The scan has no token and no side effects, and prints JSONL. The controller files and closes.\n81\t- (3) Nothing writes `.ard/` role directories. The starter goes in `internal/roles/`. ard's own `.ard/scanners/lint/` and `.ard/config.yaml` changes are a **human follow-up PR**.\n82\t- (6) Lint messages, source lines and paths come from repository content. They are treated as untrusted data, rendered only inside ```` ```text ```` fences with ```` ``` ```` neutralised to `'''` (the cve convention, see `untrusted_summary`), and inline-code spans have backticks replaced. The controller also escapes HTML comment delimiters. An `@name` in a message lands inside a fence, so it does not notify anyone.\n83\t- Code execution: golangci-lint type-checks but does not run repo code. It is built with `CGO_ENABLED=0`, so a repo config's `goplugin` custom linter cannot load. A config that asks for one fails the run, which is closed.\n84\t\n85\t**Operational risks and mitigations.**\n86\t\n87\t| Risk | Effect | Mitigation in this PR |\n88\t| --- | --- | --- |\n89\t| Output truncated, or \"new only\" mode from repo config | Mass autoclose | Forced flags (above); a unit test asserts the argv |\n90\t| Compile error, module load failure, newer `go` directive than the image | Partial results, then autoclose | `typecheck` issue or any non-zero exit fails the run. A module needing a newer Go fails with a clear message, and toolchain switching (as #98 did for cve) is a follow-up |\n91\t| golangci-lint version bump changes message text | Every fingerprint changes, so open issues autoclose, baseline entries stop matching, and new issues are filed (capped by `max_open: 3`) | Dockerfile header says: bump the version and regenerate `baseline` in the same human PR. `scan` logs the tool version and the count of unused baseline entries to stderr |\n92\t| Host mode (no Docker) uses the host's golangci-lint version | Fingerprint drift between hosts | The starter ships a Dockerfile, and `scan` logs the version |\n93\t| Worker silences rather than fixes (`//nolint`, editing `.golangci.yml`) | Issue autocloses with no fix, which inflates Gate 3 | `//nolint` directives are findings (open question 3); protect `.golangci.*` (open question 4) |\n94\t| Human adds an open finding's fingerprint to `baseline` | That issue is autoclosed as \"No longer detected\" and gets a `fixed` tombstone | Documented in the proposal: close the issue as not planned (suppression) instead of baselining it, or accept the close |\n95\t\n96\t**Split?** No. The pieces are tested together, and none of it is useful alone.\n97\t\n98\t### Decisions this PR makes (each documented in the proposal)\n99\t\n100\t1. **Engine: golangci-lint v2, Go only, for v1.** It runs once per `go.mod` (pruning `.git`, `vendor`, `node_modules` and `testdata`, like cve), with the repo's own golangci-lint config if it has one, else golangci-lint's defaults. A human-owned `golangci.yml` in the role directory overrides the repo config (`--config`) when present. A repo with no `go.mod` gives zero golangci findings and exits 0. Other ecosystems (shellcheck and others) are follow-ups (open question 2).\n101\t2. **Forced flags**, always appended after any config: `run --path-mode=abs --output.json.path=<tmp>/<n>.json --output.text.path=stderr --show-stats=false --issues-exit-code=0 --max-issues-per-linter=0 --max-same-issues=0 --new=false --new-from-rev= --new-from-merge-base= --new-from-patch= --fix=false --allow-parallel-runners ./...`.\n102\t3. **Fingerprint** (readable, no hashing, so jq alone is enough): `lint:<rule>:<path>:<msg>`.\n103\t   - `<rule>` is `FromLinter`, plus `/<code>` when `Text` starts with a check code `^[A-Z]+[0-9]+: ` (staticcheck `SA4000`, gosec `G104`, and so on), or, for `govet` and `revive` only, an analyzer name `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*: ` (for example `govet/printf`). The code prefix is removed from `<msg>`.\n104\t   - `<path>` is the repo-relative slash path: the absolute path with the physical or logical worktree root stripped, as in cve's `rel`.\n105\t   - `<msg>` is `Text` without the code prefix. Control characters are removed, whitespace runs become one space, the result is trimmed, and every standalone number (`\\b[0-9]+\\b`) becomes `N`. That keeps \"cyclomatic complexity 31\" and \"32\" one finding, and it leaves line numbers out entirely.\n106\t   - If the fingerprint would exceed 512 bytes, `<msg>` is cut by runes until it fits. A path containing a control character, or a path that alone leaves no room, fails the run with an error naming the path, which is closed.\n107\t   - **Collapse:** issues with the same fingerprint in one file become **one finding** that lists every line. A known gap: a new occurrence of an identical message in the same file is hidden while the old one is open or baselined (open question 5).\n108\t4. **Group** `<rule>:<dir>`, where `<dir>` is the path's directory or `.`. With `group_size: 20` this gives \"20 per rule and directory\".\n109\t5. **Severity:** `medium` for `govet/*`, `staticcheck/SA*`, `gosec*`, `bodyclose`, `nilerr`, `nilnesserr`, `rowserrcheck`, `sqlclosecheck` and `durationcheck`. Everything else, including `errcheck` and `nolint`, is `low`. Nothing is `high` or `critical`, and golangci's `Severity` field is ignored in v1. These are starting values to tune, like the proposal's intervals.\n110\t6. **Title:** `<rule>: <first line of original text without the code prefix> (<path>)`, one line, at most 200 runes. If it is longer, the message part is cut and ends with `…`.\n111\t7. **Body:** fixed labels plus fenced untrusted text, at most 8 KiB.\n112\t   ```\n113\t   Linter: `errcheck`   Rule: `errcheck`\n114\t   File: `internal/x/y.go`\n115\t   Lines: 6, 7            (first 20 lines, then \"and N more\")\n116\t   Reported by: golangci-lint <version>\n117\t\n118\t   Message (untrusted text from the linted code):\n119\t   ```text\n120\t   Error return value of `os.Remove` is not checked\n121\t   ```\n122\t\n123\t   Source, line 6 (untrusted):\n124\t   ```text\n125\t   \tos.Remove(\"x\")\n126\t   ```\n127\t   ```\n128\t   The message is capped at 2,000 runes and the source line at 500. `files` is `[<path>]`.\n129\t8. **`//nolint` directives are findings** (open question 3). `scan` lists `.go` files outside the pruned directories that match `//[[:space:]]*nolint`. Each matching line becomes rule `nolint`, fingerprint `lint:nolint:<path>:<trimmed, whitespace-collapsed line text>` (same collapse and 512-byte rule), group `nolint:<dir>`, severity `low`, and title `nolint: <line text> (<path>)`. The body says the directive hides linter findings: fix the finding and remove the directive, or ask a human to baseline it.\n130\t9. **Baseline.** The file is `<role dir>/baseline`, UTF-8 text. Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored. Every other line, trimmed, is one fingerprint and must start with `lint:`, else the run fails, naming the line number. Duplicate lines are fine. A finding whose fingerprint is listed is dropped. **A missing `baseline` fails the run** (open question 1) with: `lint: no baseline file: generate one with \"scan --baseline > baseline\" in the role directory and commit it (an empty file means no baseline)`.\n131\t10. **`scan --baseline`** prints a baseline of **all** current findings, ignoring any existing `baseline` file and not requiring one. It prints a header comment (tool version, \"generated by scan --baseline\", how to use it), then for each finding sorted by fingerprint a `# <title>` comment line followed by the fingerprint line. Humans run it through Docker, and the exact command goes in the Dockerfile header and the proposal.\n132\t11. **Toolchain:** the image's Go only (`GOTOOLCHAIN=local`). A module whose `go` or `toolchain` line needs a newer Go fails the run with the golangci-lint error plus `lint: <go.mod> needs a newer Go than the image's <ver>; update the lint image`. Switching toolchains like cve's #98 is a follow-up.\n133\t\n134\t### Engineer view: files and exact behaviour\n135\t\n136\t#### `internal/roles/scanners/lint/scan` (POSIX sh, mode 0755)\n137\t\n138\tThe header comment states the contract, modelled on cve's.\n139\t- The cwd is a read-only worktree. Siblings are found from `$0` (`dir=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)`).\n140\t- stdout gets JSONL **only as the last action**. Any failure exits non-zero with empty stdout.\n141\t- Nothing is written outside a `mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/ard-lint.XXXXXX\"` directory, which is removed on exit (`chmod -R u+w` first because of Go's read-only module cache).\n142\t- Exit codes: `0` success, `1` failure, `2` required tool missing (`golangci-lint`, `go`, `jq`, `find`, `grep`).\n143\t- Arguments: none, or exactly `--baseline`. Anything else is exit 1 with usage on stderr.\n144\t\n145\tSteps:\n146\t1. `need golangci-lint go jq`. Set up the temp dir and traps (`INT` exits 130, `TERM` exits 143). Point `GOCACHE`, `GOMODCACHE` and `GOPATH` at the temp dir when unset or unwritable (copy cve's loop). Always set `GOLANGCI_LINT_CACHE=$tmp/golangci`. Export `GOWORK=off GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly GOTOOLCHAIN=local`.\n147\t2. Log `golangci-lint: $(golangci-lint version --short 2>/dev/null || golangci-lint --version | head -n1)` and `go: $(go env GOVERSION)` to stderr.\n148\t3. Outside `--baseline` mode, `[ -f \"$dir/baseline\" ] || die \"<message from decision 9>\"`.\n149\t4. `cfg=` becomes `--config \"$dir/golangci.yml\"` if that file exists, with `golangci: using role config` logged. Otherwise log `golangci: repo config or defaults`.\n150\t5. Find the modules, with the same `find` prune as cve, then `LC_ALL=C sort`. For each `go.mod`:\n151\t   `(cd -- \"$mdir\" && golangci-lint run $cfg <forced flags> ./...) 2>\"$tmp/gl.err\"`. A non-zero exit means: if `gl.err` mentions the Go version, `die \"<decision 11 message>\"`, else `die \"golangci-lint failed in $manifest (exit $rc): $(tail -n 3 \"$tmp/gl.err\")\"`. On success, append `{\"module\": \"<mdir>\", \"report\": <json>}` as one line to `$tmp/gl.jsonl` (`jq -c --arg module \"$mdir\" '{module: $module, report: .}'`). Log one line per module: `golangci-lint: <go.mod>: <n> issue(s)`.\n152\t6. nolint: `find . <same prune> -name '*.go' -type f -exec grep -lE '//[[:space:]]*nolint' {} + > \"$tmp/nolint.files\"`. Here grep exit 1 (no match) is not an error, and anything above 1 is a failure. For each listed file, run `grep -nE … \"$f\" | jq -R -c --arg path \"${f#./}\" 'capture(\"^(?<line>[0-9]+):(?<text>.*)$\") | {path: $path, line: (.line|tonumber), text}' >> \"$tmp/nolint.jsonl\"`.\n153\t7. Merge: `jq -n -c` for findings, or `jq -n -r` for baseline mode, with `--arg mode findings|baseline`, `--arg root \"$(pwd -P)\"`, `--arg lroot \"$(pwd)\"`, `--arg version \"<golangci version>\"`, `--rawfile baseline \"$dir/baseline\"` (or an empty temp file in baseline mode), `--slurpfile gl \"$tmp/gl.jsonl\"`, `--slurpfile nolint \"$tmp/nolint.jsonl\"`, and `-f \"$dir/normalize.jq\"`, writing `$tmp/out`. A non-zero jq exit means `die \"normalize failed\"`, and jq's `error(...)` text reaches stderr.\n154\t8. In findings mode, log `lint: <n> finding(s), <b> baselined, <u> baseline entries unused`. `<u>` comes from `comm` over the sorted fingerprints and the sorted baseline lines, from a second `normalize.jq` call with `$mode == \"fingerprints\"` that prints every pre-baseline fingerprint raw. Then `cat \"$tmp/out\"`.\n155\t\n156\t#### `internal/roles/scanners/lint/normalize.jq` (pure, deterministic, jq 1.6+)\n157\t\n158\tHeader comment: inputs, outputs, purity (no timestamps). Definitions:\n159\t- `rel`: strip `$root/` or `$lroot/`. An absolute path left over is `error(\"lint: path outside the repository: …\")`.\n160\t- `rule_and_msg(linter; text)` returns `{rule, msg_raw}` using the code rules in decision 3.\n161\t- `norm`: remove control characters with `gsub(\"[\\\\u0000-\\\\u001f\\\\u007f]\"; \" \")`, collapse whitespace with `gsub(\"\\\\s+\"; \" \")`, trim, then `gsub(\"\\\\b[0-9]+\\\\b\"; \"N\")`. Not applied to nolint text's numbers: nolint uses only the control-character strip, collapse and trim.\n162\t- `fp(rule; path; msg)` applies the 512-byte fit with `utf8bytelength` and fails on a control character in the path.\n163\t- `fence`: `gsub(\"```\"; \"'''\")`. `code`: `gsub(\"`\"; \"'\")`.\n164\t- `sev(rule)` is the decision-5 table.\n165\t- `cands` covers every issue in every `$gl[].report.Issues`. **Any `FromLinter == \"typecheck\"` is `error(\"lint: <module>: typecheck: <first line of Text>\")`.** `$nolint[]` gives nolint candidates.\n166\t- Collapse: `group_by(.fingerprint)` merges into one finding with lines sorted and unique. Title and source come from the lowest line.\n167\t- Baseline parse: `$baseline | split(\"\\n\") | map(sub(\"\\r$\";\"\") | trim-equivalent) | map(select(. != \"\" and (startswith(\"#\")|not)))`. A remaining entry that does not start with `lint:` is `error(\"lint: baseline line <n> is not a fingerprint\")`. Line numbers come from the pre-filter index.\n168\t- Modes:\n169\t  - `findings`: findings not in the baseline, sorted by fingerprint, keys in the order `fingerprint,title,severity,group,files,body`.\n170\t  - `baseline`: the header text, then `# <title>\\n<fingerprint>` per finding.\n171\t  - `fingerprints`: every fingerprint, one per line.\n172\t\n173\t#### `internal/roles/scanners/lint/Dockerfile`\n174\t\n175\t- Header, in the style of cve's: versions and the verification date, why it builds golangci-lint from source, the bump rule (\"bump golangci-lint and regenerate every repo's `baseline` in the same PR: message text changes move fingerprints\"), the exact run and baseline commands mirroring the executor's argv:\n176\t  `docker build -t ard-lint .ard/scanners/lint && docker run --rm --user \"$(id -u):$(id -g)\" -e HOME=/tmp --tmpfs /tmp -v \"$PWD\":/work:ro -v \"$PWD/.ard/scanners/lint\":/role:ro -w /work ard-lint /role/scan --baseline > .ard/scanners/lint/baseline`.\n177\t  It also notes that the image does not copy `scan` or `normalize.jq`.\n178\t- `ARG GO_IMAGE=` the **same digest-pinned `golang:1.27.4-trixie`** as cve.\n179\t- Stage `golangci`: `RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOBIN=/out go install github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/v2/cmd/golangci-lint@${GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION}`. Use v2.15.0 (released 2026-10-16, checked locally), or the newest release at least two weeks old when implemented. Building it with the image's Go makes golangci-lint's Go version equal to the image's, so it supports every module the image can build. Integrity comes from the module proxy and the checksum database. Releases built with an older Go would refuse newer `go` directives.\n180\t- Stage `tools`: jq 1.8.2 with the same per-arch SHA-256 ARGs as cve's Dockerfile.\n181\t- Final stage: the Go image plus `/usr/local/bin/golangci-lint` and `jq`, with `ENV GOTOOLCHAIN=local` and `ENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp` (the executor's `/tmp` is a noexec tmpfs, and the caches are large).\n182\t\n183\t#### Other files\n184\t\n185\t- `internal/roles/config.yaml`: add `scanners/lint: { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }` under `overrides` with a one-line comment (\"needs a human-made `baseline` next to `scan`; see its Dockerfile\"). If open question 4 is accepted, add `\"**/.golangci.yml\"`, `\"**/.golangci.yaml\"`, `\"**/.golangci.toml\"` and `\"**/.golangci.json\"` to `protected_paths` under a \"Linter config a PR could weaken\" comment.\n186\t- `internal/roles/roles.go`: update the doc comment's role list. `ExecutableNames` is unchanged (`scan`).\n187\t- `internal/initcmd/body.go`: under \"Before you merge\", when the ops include `.ard/scanners/lint/scan`, add a bullet: \"The lint scanner fails until you commit `.ard/scanners/lint/baseline`: run the command in `.ard/scanners/lint/Dockerfile`'s header (an empty file means no baseline).\" This is fixed text only.\n188\t- `Makefile`: add a `lint-scanner-fixtures` target mirroring `cve-fixtures`: build the image, then run `sh testdata/lint/regen.sh` in it. It needs Docker and network, and is not part of `make test`.\n189\t- `internal/roles/testdata/lint/regen.sh`: builds tiny modules under a fixed temp root and runs `scan`'s exact golangci-lint command per module. It writes `gl.jsonl`, with the root replaced by `@ROOT@` and `Report.Linters` dropped to keep fixtures small (normalize.jq never reads it). It also writes `nolint.jsonl` (via the same grep and jq), an empty `baseline` unless the case has one, and `want.jsonl` from `normalize.jq`. Document \"review every `want.jsonl` diff by hand\", as cve does.\n190\t\n191\t### Tests (no network unless tagged)\n192\t\n193\tAll in `internal/roles`, table-driven, using `needTools(t, \"jq\")` and the like from cve_test.go.\n194\t\n195\t1. **`lint_test.go`: `TestLintNormalizeGolden`.** Cases live in `testdata/lint/<case>/` with `gl.jsonl`, `nolint.jsonl`, `baseline`, and either `want.jsonl` or `want.txt` or `want.err` (a substring that must appear on stderr, with a non-zero jq exit). Tests run jq exactly as `scan` does, with `/R` and `/L` roots.\n196\t   - **Real cases** (regenerated by `regen.sh`):\n197\t     - `basic`: two identical errcheck lines (collapsed), `govet/printf`, `unused`, and a `staticcheck/SA*`.\n198\t     - `nested_module`: two modules, so the path prefixes differ.\n199\t     - `repo_config_new_only`: a repo `.golangci.yml` with `issues.new: true` and `max-same-issues: 1`, run with the forced flags. The output still has every issue, which proves the flags win.\n200\t   - **Synthetic cases:**\n201\t\n202\t     | Case | What it checks |\n203\t     | --- | --- |\n204\t     | `empty` | no issues |\n205\t     | `digits_normalized` | complexity 31 and 32 give the same fingerprint |\n206\t     | `code_prefixes` | `SA4000:`, `G104:`, `printf:` on govet, a lowercase prefix on errcheck that must NOT be split |\n207\t     | `baseline_filters` | comments, blank lines, CRLF, a duplicate entry |\n208\t     | `baseline_mode` | `want.txt` |\n209\t     | `fingerprints_mode` | every fingerprint, one per line |\n210\t     | `bad_baseline_line` | `want.err`: \"baseline line 3\" |\n211\t     | `typecheck` | `want.err`: \"typecheck\" |\n212\t     | `path_outside_root` | `want.err` |\n213\t     | `control_char_path` | `want.err` |\n214\t     | `long_message` | fingerprint at most 512 bytes, title at most 200 runes, ends with `…` |\n215\t     | `untrusted_text` | ```` ``` ````, `<!-- ard:fp=x -->`, `@someone`, a backtick in the path, a multi-line `Text` |\n216\t     | `severity_table` | each medium rule plus a low one |\n217\t     | `nolint_directives` | collapse of identical lines in one file, two files |\n218\t     | `many_lines` | more than 20 occurrences, \"and N more\" |\n219\t2. **`TestLintFixtureCasesListed`**: the directories under testdata/lint equal the listed real and synthetic cases (as for cve).\n220\t3. **`TestLintWantDecodes`**: every `want.jsonl` passes `scanner.DecodeFindings` (import `internal/scanner` in the test; there is no cycle) and has no duplicate fingerprints. Every title is at most `scanner.MaxTitleRunes`, and every body is at most 64 KiB.\n221\t4. **`lint_scan_test.go`: `TestLintScanStubbed`** (sh, jq, find and grep; skip when missing). It copies `scanners/lint/{scan,normalize.jq}` to a temp role directory and builds a temp repo dir with `go.mod` files and `.go` files, then makes it read-only with `chmod -R a-w` and restores it in `t.Cleanup`. Stub `golangci-lint` and `go` scripts on a temp `PATH` write their argv and cwd to a log and print canned JSON taken from the fixtures. For `go env GOVERSION` the stub prints `go1.27.4`. Cases:\n222\t\n223\t   | Case | Expect |\n224\t   | --- | --- |\n225\t   | success | the findings; exit 0; stderr has per-module lines and the \"baseline entries unused\" count |\n226\t   | argv | each golangci call has every forced flag from decision 2, `--config <role>/golangci.yml` only when that file exists, and runs once per module in its directory, sorted |\n227\t   | golangci exits 3 | exit 1, empty stdout |\n228\t   | Go-version error text on stderr | exit 1, message names the `go.mod` |\n229\t   | typecheck issue | exit 1, empty stdout |\n230\t   | `golangci-lint` missing | exit 2 |\n231\t   | no `baseline` | exit 1, message contains `scan --baseline` |\n232\t   | `--baseline` with no baseline | exit 0, prints the baseline text |\n233\t   | bad argument | exit 1 |\n234\t   | no `go.mod`, one `.go` file with `//nolint` | golangci never called, one nolint finding |\n235\t   | read-only repo | nothing is written in the repo dir: compare a file listing before and after |\n236\t5. **`roles_test.go`.**\n237\t   - `TestFSContents` adds `scanners/lint/Dockerfile`, `scanners/lint/normalize.jq` and `scanners/lint/scan`.\n238\t   - `TestScanIsExecutableOnDisk` loops over `scanners/cve/scan` and `scanners/lint/scan`.\n239\t   - A new `TestEmbeddedLintRoleLoadsAsScanner` checks ScanPath, Autoclose, `Every == 24h`, `MaxOpen == 3`, `GroupSize == 20`, the Dockerfile, and `Extra == [normalize.jq]`.\n240\t   - If open question 4 is accepted, assert the `.golangci.*` protected paths with `config.Protected` on a sample path.\n241\t6. **`internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`**: add the three lint files to `starterTree`, assert `scan` is `100755`, assert `cres.Role(KindScanner, \"lint\")` overrides and the `ard:scanner:lint` label, and assert the body contains the baseline bullet.\n242\t7. **Integration (`//go:build integration`).**\n243\t   - `lint_integration_test.go` (host golangci-lint and go; skip if absent) runs the real `scan` on a temp module with errcheck, govet printf, unused, a `//nolint` and a repo `.golangci.yml` with `issues.new: true`. It checks: findings appear; `scan --baseline > baseline` followed by `scan` gives empty stdout; adding one new unchecked call gives exactly one finding.\n244\t   - `lint_docker_integration_test.go` builds `scanners/lint` and runs it with the existing `scanRunArgs` helper (same package and tag as cve's; generalise its doc comment) on a `go 1.27` module, checking the findings. A `go 1.99` module must exit 1 with the decision 11 message.\n245\t\n246\t### Proposal and docs updates (same PR)\n247\t\n248\t- **docs/proposal.md, Scanners.**\n249\t  - Table row `lint`: Engine becomes \"golangci-lint per Go module (the repo's config, or the role's `golangci.yml`), plus `//nolint` directives, minus the role directory's `baseline`\".\n250\t  - Add a paragraph **\"The lint scanner\"** after the cve one, covering decisions 1 to 11 in prose: forced flags and why (autoclose safety), fail-closed cases, the fingerprint and collapse with its known gap, the group key, the severity table, the baseline file, location and format, `scan --baseline`, the \"baseline an open finding closes it as completed; close it as not planned instead\" note, version-bump churn, and Go-only v1.\n251\t- **docs/proposal.md, Configuration**, in the `ard init` paragraph (line ~407): add `scanners/lint` to the starter role list and the lint override to \"the … overrides\". Add the PR body's baseline step. If accepted, add the `.golangci.*` entries wherever the protected-path defaults are listed.\n252\t- **CLAUDE.md, Layout**: both `internal/roles/` lines add `scanners/lint`.\n253\t\n254\t### Out of scope (file as follow-ups)\n255\t\n256\t- Linters for other ecosystems (shellcheck, eslint, ruff, hadolint), or a generic SARIF adapter.\n257\t- Toolchain switching for modules newer than the image's Go (the cve #98 mechanism).\n258\t- A count-aware baseline, so a new identical occurrence in the same file surfaces.\n259\t- An `ard` subcommand to generate the baseline.\n260\t- Routing lint issues to a cheaper worker model (proposal: Haiku for lint work), which needs a lint-specific worker role.\n261\t- Honouring golangci-lint's `Severity` field.\n262\t- Committing scanner logs (an existing follow-up).\n263\t\n264\t### Human follow-up PR (ard's own `.ard/`, not doable by ard or this PR)\n265\t\n266\tAfter this merges, a human:\n267\t1. Copies `internal/roles/scanners/lint/{scan,normalize.jq,Dockerfile}` to `.ard/scanners/lint/`, keeping `scan` at `100755`.\n268\t2. Builds the image and generates `.ard/scanners/lint/baseline` from `main` with the Dockerfile header's command. Expect about 184 golangci entries plus the `//nolint` lines. Consider leaving the two `staticcheck/SA4000` entries out so they file as real issues.\n269\t3. Adds `scanners/lint: { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }` to `.ard/config.yaml`, and the `.golangci.*` protected paths if open question 4 is accepted.\n270\t4. Runs `ard config check` and `ard labels sync` (for `ard:scanner:lint`).\n271\t\n272\t### Open questions for the human\n273\t\n274\t1. **Missing `baseline` file.**\n275\t   - (a) Fail closed until a human commits one (an empty file means none).\n276\t   - (b) Treat it as empty.\n277\t   - (c) Ship an empty `baseline` in the starter.\n278\t\n279\t   **Recommend (a).** \"Beyond a committed baseline\" then always reflects a human decision, and `ard init` repos never get a surprise first run of 3×20 issues. The cost is a recorded failure every 24 h until the file exists, with a message naming the fix.\n280\t2. **Linter scope for v1.**\n281\t   - (a) Go via golangci-lint only.\n282\t   - (b) Add shellcheck now (ard has shell scripts: `scan`, `regen.sh`, `deploy/*.sh`).\n283\t   - (c) A pluggable SARIF-based design.\n284\t\n285\t   **Recommend (a)**, with (b) as the first follow-up issue. normalize.jq's candidate stage is the only part shellcheck would add to.\n286\t3. **Report `//nolint` directives as findings?** (a) Yes (decision 8). (b) No, and rely on eng-review. **Recommend (a).** Without it, a worker can close a lint issue by suppressing it, and that counts towards Gate 3's \"merged with no human code edits\". It is about 30 lines of shell and jq.\n287\t4. **Protect golangci-lint config.**\n288\t   - Add `**/.golangci.{yml,yaml,toml,json}` to the starter's `protected_paths` (and ard's own, in the follow-up)? **Recommend yes.** Disabling a linter in config otherwise silently autocloses its issues. It only takes effect once the merger (#46 PR B) enforces protected paths.\n289\t   - Keep the role-directory `golangci.yml` override? **Recommend yes**, as an optional human-owned file.\n290\t5. **Collapsing identical messages in one file.**\n291\t   - (a) Collapse into one finding.\n292\t   - (b) Per-occurrence fingerprints with an index (`#2`), which renumber when an earlier one is fixed.\n293\t   - (c) A count-aware baseline.\n294\t\n295\t   **Recommend (a) now and (c) as a follow-up if the gap shows up.** (b) churns fingerprints on unrelated fixes.\n296\t6. **Severity table (decision 5).** Two levels, `medium` for bug-class rules and `low` for the rest. Confirm, or name rules to raise. It affects only filing order and suppression re-raise.\n297\t\n298\t### Done when\n299\t\n300\t- [ ] `scanners/lint/{scan,normalize.jq,Dockerfile}` are embedded, and `scan` is 0755 on disk and in `ard init`'s commit\n301\t- [ ] Starter `config.yaml` has the lint override (plus the `.golangci.*` protected paths if open question 4 is accepted). `ard init`'s PR body has the baseline step\n302\t- [ ] Golden, stubbed-scan, roles and initcmd tests pass with `make lint test`. `go test -tags integration ./internal/roles/` passes locally with golangci-lint and Docker\n303\t- [ ] `make lint-scanner-fixtures` regenerates the real cases with no diff\n304\t- [ ] Proposal (Scanners paragraph and table, `ard init` paragraph) and CLAUDE.md layout updated\n305\t- [ ] Follow-up issues filed: shellcheck, toolchain switching, count-aware baseline, and the human `.ard/scanners/lint/` PR for ard itself\n306\t\n307\t### Resolved open questions (owner, 2026-11-23)\n308\tThe owner accepted the plan's recommended answer for every open question above:\n309\t1. Missing `baseline` file: fail closed until a human commits one; an empty file means none (option a).\n310\t2. Linter scope for v1: Go via golangci-lint only; shellcheck is the first follow-up issue (option a).\n311\t3. `//nolint` directives: reported as findings (decision 8).\n312\t4. golangci-lint config: add `**/.golangci.{yml,yaml,toml,json}` to the starter's `protected_paths` (and ard's own in the follow-up), and keep the optional human-owned role-directory `golangci.yml` override.\n313\t5. Identical messages in one file: collapse into one finding now; a count-aware baseline as a follow-up if the gap shows up (option a).\n314\t6. Severity table: two levels, `medium` for bug-class rules and `low` for the rest, as in decision 5.\n315\t\n316\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5eb0b10-10f7-42ca-8b7a-846dd3a3e8b7","uuid":"9a3d73e1-13db-4ca6-9a69-f0da40ddd952","timestamp":"2026-11-23T21:20:10.944Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/ard-home/.claude/projects/-Users-al--ard-work-albertcbrown-ard-01M854FBGX7VKDVYP9DX1ZXP1S/f1a22598-6ed7-4e0c-96bb-10397288aa78/tool-results/b3cvr8ncu.txt","content":"?? .ard-input/\ninternal/roles:\nconfig.yaml\ncve_docker_integration_test.go\ncve_integration_test.go\ncve_test.go\ndocs_docker_integration_test.go\ndocs_test.go\neng_review_test.go\nengineer_test.go\nerrcodes_integration_test.go\nerrcodes_test.go\nlead_test.go\nlicense_review_integration_test.go\nlicense_review_test.go\nmissing_tests_test.go\nreviewers\nroles.go\nroles_test.go\nscanner_guard_test.go\nscanners\nsecurity_review_test.go\ntestdata\ntriage\nworker_engineer_test.go\nworkers\n\ninternal/roles/scanners/cve:\nDockerfile\nmerge.jq\nscan\n\ninternal/roles/scanners/docs:\nDockerfile\ndocscan.go\nscan\n\ninternal/roles/scanners/error-codes:\nDockerfile\nerrcodes.jq\nscan\n\ninternal/roles/scanners/missing-tests:\nmissingtests.go\n\ninternal/roles/testdata:\ncve\ndocs\nlts\nmissing-tests\n\n**Dependencies.** #23 (the scanner pipeline) is closed, and that is the only hard dependency. Do not wait for #41, #42 or #46: this change touches none of their code. It follows the pattern of #24 (`scanners/cve`): a `scan` script, a jq program, a pinned Dockerfile, golden fixtures and integration tests behind the `integration` build tag. Sibling scanner issues (#47, #49, #50) can copy the same layout, and no shared code is needed now.\n\n### What was checked on main (2026-11-23)\n\n- `ExecEngine.Scan` (internal/scanner/engine_exec.go) runs `<role dir>/scan` with no arguments. The cwd is a **read-only worktree detached at the config SHA**, the role directory (including its `Extra` files) is mounted read-only, and the run has no GitHub token and no model key, but has network egress. Only stdout is decoded, by the strict `scanner.DecodeFindings`. Any non-zero exit discards the run. A role with a `Dockerfile` runs in that image. A deterministic scanner has `TrustedInput`, so it gets no host-mode warning.\n- `config` discovers `scanners/lint` from the presence of an executable `scan`. `Autoclose` defaults to true for a `scan` scanner. Overrides go in `config.yaml`. The proposal's Configuration example already carries `scanners/lint: { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }`.\n- **golangci-lint v2.15.0 behaviour, checked by hand on a scratch module.** Each item below drives a decision.\n  - With the defaults `max-issues-per-linter: 50` and `max-same-issues: 3`, output is truncated, so findings over the caps would vanish and be **autoclosed**. Both must be forced to `0`.\n  - A repo config with `issues.new: true` (or `new-from-rev`, `new-from-merge-base`, `new-from-patch`) makes a clean read-only checkout report **zero issues**. That would autoclose every lint issue. The flags `--new=false --new-from-rev= --new-from-merge-base= --new-from-patch=` override the config (verified).\n  - With `--issues-exit-code=0`, a compile error comes back as an issue with `FromLinter: \"typecheck\"` and exit 0. It must fail the run.\n  - `--path-mode=abs` gives absolute filenames, which makes multi-module path handling simple.\n  - JSON shape: `{\"Issues\":[{\"FromLinter\",\"Text\",\"Severity\",\"SourceLines\":[..],\"Pos\":{\"Filename\",\"Line\",\"Column\"}}],\"Report\":{...}}`.\n- **ard itself today, golangci-lint v2.15.0 defaults** (errcheck, govet, ineffassign, staticcheck, unused): 300 raw issues, 184 distinct after collapsing (see fingerprint). 273 are errcheck (156 of those in `_test.go`), 2 are `staticcheck SA4000` in `internal/servecmd/reaping_test.go` (look like real bugs), and there are 10 `//nolint` directives. ard's own enablement therefore needs a baseline (see Human follow-up).\n\n### Tech lead view\n\n**Architecture fit.** A deterministic scanner fits the existing pipeline and needs **no Go code change in the controller**. All dedupe, grouping, filing, autoclose and suppression stay in `internal/scanner`. The role directory holds:\n\n```\ninternal/roles/scanners/lint/\n  scan          # sh, 0755: runs golangci-lint per Go module, finds //nolint, calls normalize.jq\n  normalize.jq  # pure: golangci-lint JSON + nolint lines + baseline -> findings JSONL (or baseline text)\n  Dockerfile    # pinned golang base (same digest as cve) + golangci-lint built with it + jq\n```\n\nThe `baseline` is **not** shipped in the starter (see open question 1). It is a human-owned file a repo adds next to `scan`. Because it lives under `.ard/scanners/`, it is a protected path and outside every agent's write allowlist. A worker therefore cannot \"fix\" a lint issue by baselining it. That is the main reason to keep it in the role directory and not at the repo root.\n\n**Invariants (CLAUDE.md).**\n- (1)(2) The scan has no token and no side effects, and prints JSONL. The controller files and closes.\n- (3) Nothing writes `.ard/` role directories. The starter goes in `internal/roles/`. ard's own `.ard/scanners/lint/` and `.ard/config.yaml` changes are a **human follow-up PR**.\n- (6) Lint messages, source lines and paths come from repository content. They are treated as untrusted data, rendered only inside ```` ```text ```` fences with ```` ``` ```` neutralised to `'''` (the cve convention, see `untrusted_summary`), and inline-code spans have backticks replaced. The controller also escapes HTML comment delimiters. An `@name` in a message lands inside a fence, so it does not notify anyone.\n- Code execution: golangci-lint type-checks but does not run repo code. It is built with `CGO_ENABLED=0`, so a repo config's `goplugin` custom linter cannot load. A config that asks for one fails the run, which is closed.\n\n**Operational risks and mitigations.**\n\n| Risk | Effect | Mitigation in this PR |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Output truncated, or \"new only\" mode from repo config | Mass autoclose | Forced flags (above); a unit test asserts the argv |\n| Compile error, module load failure, newer `go` directive than the image | Partial results, then autoclose | `typecheck` issue or any non-zero exit fails the run. A module needing a newer Go fails with a clear message, and toolchain switching (as #98 did for cve) is a follow-up |\n| golangci-lint version bump changes message text | Every fingerprint changes, so open issues autoclose, baseline entries stop matching, and new issues are filed (capped by `max_open: 3`) | Dockerfile header says: bump the version and regenerate `baseline` in the same human PR. `scan` logs the tool version and the count of unused baseline entries to stderr |\n| Host mode (no Docker) uses the host's golangci-lint version | Fingerprint drift between hosts | The starter ships a Dockerfile, and `scan` logs the version |\n| Worker silences rather than fixes (`//nolint`, editing `.golangci.yml`) | Issue autocloses with no fix, which inflates Gate 3 | `//nolint` directives are findings (open question 3); protect `.golangci.*` (open question 4) |\n| Human adds an open finding's fingerprint to `baseline` | That issue is autoclosed as \"No longer detected\" and gets a `fixed` tombstone | Documented in the proposal: close the issue as not planned (suppression) instead of baselining it, or accept the close |\n\n**Split?** No. The pieces are tested together, and none of it is useful alone.\n\n### Decisions this PR makes (each documented in the proposal)\n\n1. **Engine: golangci-lint v2, Go only, for v1.** It runs once per `go.mod` (pruning `.git`, `vendor`, `node_modules` and `testdata`, like cve), with the repo's own golangci-lint config if it has one, else golangci-lint's defaults. A human-owned `golangci.yml` in the role directory overrides the repo config (`--config`) when present. A repo with no `go.mod` gives zero golangci findings and exits 0. Other ecosystems (shellcheck and others) are follow-ups (open question 2).\n2. **Forced flags**, always appended after any config: `run --path-mode=abs --output.json.path=<tmp>/<n>.json --output.text.path=stderr --show-stats=false --issues-exit-code=0 --max-issues-per-linter=0 --max-same-issues=0 --new=false --new-from-rev= --new-from-merge-base= --new-from-patch= --fix=false --allow-parallel-runners ./...`.\n3. **Fingerprint** (readable, no hashing, so jq alone is enough): `lint:<rule>:<path>:<msg>`.\n   - `<rule>` is `FromLinter`, plus `/<code>` when `Text` starts with a check code `^[A-Z]+[0-9]+: ` (staticcheck `SA4000`, gosec `G104`, and so on), or, for `govet` and `revive` only, an analyzer name `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*: ` (for example `govet/printf`). The code prefix is removed from `<msg>`.\n   - `<path>` is the repo-relative slash path: the absolute path with the physical or logical worktree root stripped, as in cve's `rel`.\n   - `<msg>` is `Text` without the code prefix. Control characters are removed, whitespace runs become one space, the result is trimmed, and every standalone number (`\\b[0-9]+\\b`) becomes `N`. That keeps \"cyclomatic complexity 31\" and \"32\" one finding, and it leaves line numbers out entirely.\n   - If the fingerprint would exceed 512 bytes, `<msg>` is cut by runes until it fits. A path containing a control character, or a path that alone leaves no room, fails the run with an error naming the path, which is closed.\n   - **Collapse:** issues with the same fingerprint in one file become **one finding** that lists every line. A known gap: a new occurrence of an identical message in the same file is hidden while the old one is open or baselined (open question 5).\n4. **Group** `<rule>:<dir>`, where `<dir>` is the path's directory or `.`. With `group_size: 20` this gives \"20 per rule and directory\".\n5. **Severity:** `medium` for `govet/*`, `staticcheck/SA*`, `gosec*`, `bodyclose`, `nilerr`, `nilnesserr`, `rowserrcheck`, `sqlclosecheck` and `durationcheck`. Everything else, including `errcheck` and `nolint`, is `low`. Nothing is `high` or `critical`, and golangci's `Severity` field is ignored in v1. These are starting values to tune, like the proposal's intervals.\n6. **Title:** `<rule>: <first line of original text without the code prefix> (<path>)`, one line, at most 200 runes. If it is longer, the message part is cut and ends with `…`.\n7. **Body:** fixed labels plus fenced untrusted text, at most 8 KiB.\n   ```\n   Linter: `errcheck`   Rule: `errcheck`\n   File: `internal/x/y.go`\n   Lines: 6, 7            (first 20 lines, then \"and N more\")\n   Reported by: golangci-lint <version>\n\n   Message (untrusted text from the linted code):\n   ```text\n   Error return value of `os.Remove` is not checked\n   ```\n\n   Source, line 6 (untrusted):\n   ```text\n   \tos.Remove(\"x\")\n   ```\n   ```\n   The message is capped at 2,000 runes and the source line at 500. `files` is `[<path>]`.\n8. **`//nolint` directives are findings** (open question 3). `scan` lists `.go` files outside the pruned directories that match `//[[:space:]]*nolint`. Each matching line becomes rule `nolint`, fingerprint `lint:nolint:<path>:<trimmed, whitespace-collapsed line text>` (same collapse and 512-byte rule), group `nolint:<dir>`, severity `low`, and title `nolint: <line text> (<path>)`. The body says the directive hides linter findings: fix the finding and remove the directive, or ask a human to baseline it.\n9. **Baseline.** The file is `<role dir>/baseline`, UTF-8 text. Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored. Every other line, trimmed, is one fingerprint and must start with `lint:`, else the run fails, naming the line number. Duplicate lines are fine. A finding whose fingerprint is listed is dropped. **A missing `baseline` fails the run** (open question 1) with: `lint: no baseline file: generate one with \"scan --baseline > baseline\" in the role directory and commit it (an empty file means no baseline)`.\n10. **`scan --baseline`** prints a baseline of **all** current findings, ignoring any existing `baseline` file and not requiring one. It prints a header comment (tool version, \"generated by scan --baseline\", how to use it), then for each finding sorted by fingerprint a `# <title>` comment line followed by the fingerprint line. Humans run it through Docker, and the exact command goes in the Dockerfile header and the proposal.\n11. **Toolchain:** the image's Go only (`GOTOOLCHAIN=local`). A module whose `go` or `toolchain` line needs a newer Go fails the run with the golangci-lint error plus `lint: <go.mod> needs a newer Go than the image's <ver>; update the lint image`. Switching toolchains like cve's #98 is a follow-up.\n\n### Engineer view: files and exact behaviour\n\n#### `internal/roles/scanners/lint/scan` (POSIX sh, mode 0755)\n\nThe header comment states the contract, modelled on cve's.\n- The cwd is a read-only worktree. Siblings are found from `$0` (`dir=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)`).\n- stdout gets JSONL **only as the last action**. Any failure exits non-zero with empty stdout.\n- Nothing is written outside a `mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/ard-lint.XXXXXX\"` directory, which is removed on exit (`chmod -R u+w` first because of Go's read-only module cache).\n- Exit codes: `0` success, `1` failure, `2` required tool missing (`golangci-lint`, `go`, `jq`, `find`, `grep`).\n- Arguments: none, or exactly `--baseline`. Anything else is exit 1 with usage on stderr.\n\nSteps:\n1. `need golangci-lint go jq`. Set up the temp dir and traps (`INT` exits 130, `TERM` exits 143). Point `GOCACHE`, `GOMODCACHE` and `GOPATH` at the temp dir when unset or unwritable (copy cve's loop). Always set `GOLANGCI_LINT_CACHE=$tmp/golangci`. Export `GOWORK=off GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly GOTOOLCHAIN=local`.\n2. Log `golangci-lint: $(golangci-lint version --short 2>/dev/null || golangci-lint --version | head -n1)` and `go: $(go env GOVERSION)` to stderr.\n3. Outside `--baseline` mode, `[ -f \"$dir/baseline\" ] || die \"<message from decision 9>\"`.\n4. `cfg=` becomes `--config \"$dir/golangci.yml\"` if that file exists, with `golangci: using role config` logged. Otherwise log `golangci: repo config or defaults`.\n5. Find the modules, with the same `find` prune as cve, then `LC_ALL=C sort`. For each `go.mod`:\n   `(cd -- \"$mdir\" && golangci-lint run $cfg <forced flags> ./...) 2>\"$tmp/gl.err\"`. A non-zero exit means: if `gl.err` mentions the Go version, `die \"<decision 11 message>\"`, else `die \"golangci-lint failed in $manifest (exit $rc): $(tail -n 3 \"$tmp/gl.err\")\"`. On success, append `{\"module\": \"<mdir>\", \"report\": <json>}` as one line to `$tmp/gl.jsonl` (`jq -c --arg module \"$mdir\" '{module: $module, report: .}'`). Log one line per module: `golangci-lint: <go.mod>: <n> issue(s)`.\n6. nolint: `find . <same prune> -name '*.go' -type f -exec grep -lE '//[[:space:]]*nolint' {} + > \"$tmp/nolint.files\"`. Here grep exit 1 (no match) is not an error, and anything above 1 is a failure. For each listed file, run `grep -nE … \"$f\" | jq -R -c --arg path \"${f#./}\" 'capture(\"^(?<line>[0-9]+):(?<text>.*)$\") | {path: $path, line: (.line|tonumber), text}' >> \"$tmp/nolint.jsonl\"`.\n7. Merge: `jq -n -c` for findings, or `jq -n -r` for baseline mode, with `--arg mode findings|baseline`, `--arg root \"$(pwd -P)\"`, `--arg lroot \"$(pwd)\"`, `--arg version \"<golangci version>\"`, `--rawfile baseline \"$dir/baseline\"` (or an empty temp file in baseline mode), `--slurpfile gl \"$tmp/gl.jsonl\"`, `--slurpfile nolint \"$tmp/nolint.jsonl\"`, and `-f \"$dir/normalize.jq\"`, writing `$tmp/out`. A non-zero jq exit means `die \"normalize failed\"`, and jq's `error(...)` text reaches stderr.\n8. In findings mode, log `lint: <n> finding(s), <b> baselined, <u> baseline entries unused`. `<u>` comes from `comm` over the sorted fingerprints and the sorted baseline lines, from a second `normalize.jq` call with `$mode == \"fingerprints\"` that prints every pre-baseline fingerprint raw. Then `cat \"$tmp/out\"`.\n\n#### `internal/roles/scanners/lint/normalize.jq` (pure, deterministic, jq 1.6+)\n\nHeader comment: inputs, outputs, purity (no timestamps). Definitions:\n- `rel`: strip `$root/` or `$lroot/`. An absolute path left over is `error(\"lint: path outside the repository: …\")`.\n- `rule_and_msg(linter; text)` returns `{rule, msg_raw}` using the code rules in decision 3.\n- `norm`: remove control characters with `gsub(\"[\\\\u0000-\\\\u001f\\\\u007f]\"; \" \")`, collapse whitespace with `gsub(\"\\\\s+\"; \" \")`, trim, then `gsub(\"\\\\b[0-9]+\\\\b\"; \"N\")`. Not applied to nolint text's numbers: nolint uses only the control-character strip, collapse and trim.\n- `fp(rule; path; msg)` applies the 512-byte fit with `utf8bytelength` and fails on a control character in the path.\n- `fence`: `gsub(\"```\"; \"'''\")`. `code`: `gsub(\"`\"; \"'\")`.\n- `sev(rule)` is the decision-5 table.\n- `cands` covers every issue in every `$gl[].report.Issues`. **Any `FromLinter == \"typecheck\"` is `error(\"lint: <module>: typecheck: <first line of Text>\")`.** `$nolint[]` gives nolint candidates.\n- Collapse: `group_by(.fingerprint)` merges into one finding with lines sorted and unique. Title and source come from the lowest line.\n- Baseline parse: `$baseline | split(\"\\n\") | map(sub(\"\\r$\";\"\") | trim-equivalent) | map(select(. != \"\" and (startswith(\"#\")|not)))`. A remaining entry that does not start with `lint:` is `error(\"lint: baseline line <n> is not a fingerprint\")`. Line numbers come from the pre-filter index.\n- Modes:\n  - `findings`: findings not in the baseline, sorted by fingerprint, keys in the order `fingerprint,title,severity,group,files,body`.\n  - `baseline`: the header text, then `# <title>\\n<fingerprint>` per finding.\n  - `fingerprints`: every fingerprint, one per line.\n\n#### `internal/roles/scanners/lint/Dockerfile`\n\n- Header, in the style of cve's: versions and the verification date, why it builds golangci-lint from source, the bump rule (\"bump golangci-lint and regenerate every repo's `baseline` in the same PR: message text changes move fingerprints\"), the exact run and baseline commands mirroring the executor's argv:\n  `docker build -t ard-lint .ard/scanners/lint && docker run --rm --user \"$(id -u):$(id -g)\" -e HOME=/tmp --tmpfs /tmp -v \"$PWD\":/work:ro -v \"$PWD/.ard/scanners/lint\":/role:ro -w /work ard-lint /role/scan --baseline > .ard/scanners/lint/baseline`.\n  It also notes that the image does not copy `scan` or `normalize.jq`.\n- `ARG GO_IMAGE=` the **same digest-pinned `golang:1.27.4-trixie`** as cve.\n- Stage `golangci`: `RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOBIN=/out go install github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/v2/cmd/golangci-lint@${GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION}`. Use v2.15.0 (released 2026-10-16, checked locally), or the newest release at least two weeks old when implemented. Building it with the image's Go makes golangci-lint's Go version equal to the image's, so it supports every module the image can build. Integrity comes from the module proxy and the checksum database. Releases built with an older Go would refuse newer `go` directives.\n- Stage `tools`: jq 1.8.2 with the same per-arch SHA-256 ARGs as cve's Dockerfile.\n- Final stage: the Go image plus `/usr/local/bin/golangci-lint` and `jq`, with `ENV GOTOOLCHAIN=local` and `ENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp` (the executor's `/tmp` is a noexec tmpfs, and the caches are large).\n\n#### Other files\n\n- `internal/roles/config.yaml`: add `scanners/lint: { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }` under `overrides` with a one-line comment (\"needs a human-made `baseline` next to `scan`; see its Dockerfile\"). If open question 4 is accepted, add `\"**/.golangci.yml\"`, `\"**/.golangci.yaml\"`, `\"**/.golangci.toml\"` and `\"**/.golangci.json\"` to `protected_paths` under a \"Linter config a PR could weaken\" comment.\n- `internal/roles/roles.go`: update the doc comment's role list. `ExecutableNames` is unchanged (`scan`).\n- `internal/initcmd/body.go`: under \"Before you merge\", when the ops include `.ard/scanners/lint/scan`, add a bullet: \"The lint scanner fails until you commit `.ard/scanners/lint/baseline`: run the command in `.ard/scanners/lint/Dockerfile`'s header (an empty file means no baseline).\" This is fixed text only.\n- `Makefile`: add a `lint-scanner-fixtures` target mirroring `cve-fixtures`: build the image, then run `sh testdata/lint/regen.sh` in it. It needs Docker and network, and is not part of `make test`.\n- `internal/roles/testdata/lint/regen.sh`: builds tiny modules under a fixed temp root and runs `scan`'s exact golangci-lint command per module. It writes `gl.jsonl`, with the root replaced by `@ROOT@` and `Report.Linters` dropped to keep fixtures small (normalize.jq never reads it). It also writes `nolint.jsonl` (via the same grep and jq), an empty `baseline` unless the case has one, and `want.jsonl` from `normalize.jq`. Document \"review every `want.jsonl` diff by hand\", as cve does.\n\n### Tests (no network unless tagged)\n\nAll in `internal/roles`, table-driven, using `needTools(t, \"jq\")` and the like from cve_test.go.\n\n1. **`lint_test.go`: `TestLintNormalizeGolden`.** Cases live in `testdata/lint/<case>/` with `gl.jsonl`, `nolint.jsonl`, `baseline`, and either `want.jsonl` or `want.txt` or `want.err` (a substring that must appear on stderr, with a non-zero jq exit). Tests run jq exactly as `scan` does, with `/R` and `/L` roots.\n   - **Real cases** (regenerated by `regen.sh`):\n     - `basic`: two identical errcheck lines (collapsed), `govet/printf`, `unused`, and a `staticcheck/SA*`.\n     - `nested_module`: two modules, so the path prefixes differ.\n     - `repo_config_new_only`: a repo `.golangci.yml` with `issues.new: true` and `max-same-issues: 1`, run with the forced flags. The output still has every issue, which proves the flags win.\n   - **Synthetic cases:**\n\n     | Case | What it checks |\n     | --- | --- |\n     | `empty` | no issues |\n     | `digits_normalized` | complexity 31 and 32 give the same fingerprint |\n     | `code_prefixes` | `SA4000:`, `G104:`, `printf:` on govet, a lowercase prefix on errcheck that must NOT be split |\n     | `baseline_filters` | comments, blank lines, CRLF, a duplicate entry |\n     | `baseline_mode` | `want.txt` |\n     | `fingerprints_mode` | every fingerprint, one per line |\n     | `bad_baseline_line` | `want.err`: \"baseline line 3\" |\n     | `typecheck` | `want.err`: \"typecheck\" |\n     | `path_outside_root` | `want.err` |\n     | `control_char_path` | `want.err` |\n     | `long_message` | fingerprint at most 512 bytes, title at most 200 runes, ends with `…` |\n     | `untrusted_text` | ```` ``` ````, `<!-- ard:fp=x -->`, `@someone`, a backtick in the path, a multi-line `Text` |\n     | `severity_table` | each medium rule plus a low one |\n     | `nolint_directives` | collapse of identical lines in one file, two files |\n     | `many_lines` | more than 20 occurrences, \"and N more\" |\n2. **`TestLintFixtureCasesListed`**: the directories under testdata/lint equal the listed real and synthetic cases (as for cve).\n3. **`TestLintWantDecodes`**: every `want.jsonl` passes `scanner.DecodeFindings` (import `internal/scanner` in the test; there is no cycle) and has no duplicate fingerprints. Every title is at most `scanner.MaxTitleRunes`, and every body is at most 64 KiB.\n4. **`lint_scan_test.go`: `TestLintScanStubbed`** (sh, jq, find and grep; skip when missing). It copies `scanners/lint/{scan,normalize.jq}` to a temp role directory and builds a temp repo dir with `go.mod` files and `.go` files, then makes it read-only with `chmod -R a-w` and restores it in `t.Cleanup`. Stub `golangci-lint` and `go` scripts on a temp `PATH` write their argv and cwd to a log and print canned JSON taken from the fixtures. For `go env GOVERSION` the stub prints `go1.27.4`. Cases:\n\n   | Case | Expect |\n   | --- | --- |\n   | success | the findings; exit 0; stderr has per-module lines and the \"baseline entries unused\" count |\n   | argv | each golangci call has every forced flag from decision 2, `--config <role>/golangci.yml` only when that file exists, and runs once per module in its directory, sorted |\n   | golangci exits 3 | exit 1, empty stdout |\n   | Go-version error text on stderr | exit 1, message names the `go.mod` |\n   | typecheck issue | exit 1, empty stdout |\n   | `golangci-lint` missing | exit 2 |\n   | no `baseline` | exit 1, message contains `scan --baseline` |\n   | `--baseline` with no baseline | exit 0, prints the baseline text |\n   | bad argument | exit 1 |\n   | no `go.mod`, one `.go` file with `//nolint` | golangci never called, one nolint finding |\n   | read-only repo | nothing is written in the repo dir: compare a file listing before and after |\n5. **`roles_test.go`.**\n   - `TestFSContents` adds `scanners/lint/Dockerfile`, `scanners/lint/normalize.jq` and `scanners/lint/scan`.\n   - `TestScanIsExecutableOnDisk` loops over `scanners/cve/scan` and `scanners/lint/scan`.\n   - A new `TestEmbeddedLintRoleLoadsAsScanner` checks ScanPath, Autoclose, `Every == 24h`, `MaxOpen == 3`, `GroupSize == 20`, the Dockerfile, and `Extra == [normalize.jq]`.\n   - If open question 4 is accepted, assert the `.golangci.*` protected paths with `config.Protected` on a sample path.\n6. **`internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`**: add the three lint files to `starterTree`, assert `scan` is `100755`, assert `cres.Role(KindScanner, \"lint\")` overrides and the `ard:scanner:lint` label, and assert the body contains the baseline bullet.\n7. **Integration (`//go:build integration`).**\n   - `lint_integration_test.go` (host golangci-lint and go; skip if absent) runs the real `scan` on a temp module with errcheck, govet printf, unused, a `//nolint` and a repo `.golangci.yml` with `issues.new: true`. It checks: findings appear; `scan --baseline > baseline` followed by `scan` gives empty stdout; adding one new unchecked call gives exactly one finding.\n   - `lint_docker_integration_test.go` builds `scanners/lint` and runs it with the existing `scanRunArgs` helper (same package and tag as cve's; generalise its doc comment) on a `go 1.27` module, checking the findings. A `go 1.99` module must exit 1 with the decision 11 message.\n\n### Proposal and docs updates (same PR)\n\n- **docs/proposal.md, Scanners.**\n  - Table row `lint`: Engine becomes \"golangci-lint per Go module (the repo's config, or the role's `golangci.yml`), plus `//nolint` directives, minus the role directory's `baseline`\".\n  - Add a paragraph **\"The lint scanner\"** after the cve one, covering decisions 1 to 11 in prose: forced flags and why (autoclose safety), fail-closed cases, the fingerprint and collapse with its known gap, the group key, the severity table, the baseline file, location and format, `scan --baseline`, the \"baseline an open finding closes it as completed; close it as not planned instead\" note, version-bump churn, and Go-only v1.\n- **docs/proposal.md, Configuration**, in the `ard init` paragraph (line ~407): add `scanners/lint` to the starter role list and the lint override to \"the … overrides\". Add the PR body's baseline step. If accepted, add the `.golangci.*` entries wherever the protected-path defaults are listed.\n- **CLAUDE.md, Layout**: both `internal/roles/` lines add `scanners/lint`.\n\n### Out of scope (file as follow-ups)\n\n- Linters for other ecosystems (shellcheck, eslint, ruff, hadolint), or a generic SARIF adapter.\n- Toolchain switching for modules newer than the image's Go (the cve #98 mechanism).\n- A count-aware baseline, so a new identical occurrence in the same file surfaces.\n- An `ard` subcommand to generate the baseline.\n- Routing lint issues to a cheaper worker model (proposal: Haiku for lint work), which needs a lint-specific worker role.\n- Honouring golangci-lint's `Severity` field.\n- Committing scanner logs (an existing follow-up).\n\n### Human follow-up PR (ard's own `.ard/`, not doable by ard or this PR)\n\nAfter this merges, a human:\n1. Copies `internal/roles/scanners/lint/{scan,normalize.jq,Dockerfile}` to `.ard/scanners/lint/`, keeping `scan` at `100755`.\n2. Builds the image and generates `.ard/scanners/lint/baseline` from `main` with the Dockerfile header's command. Expect about 184 golangci entries plus the `//nolint` lines. Consider leaving the two `staticcheck/SA4000` entries out so they file as real issues.\n3. Adds `scanners/lint: { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }` to `.ard/config.yaml`, and the `.golangci.*` protected paths if open question 4 is accepted.\n4. Runs `ard config check` and `ard labels sync` (for `ard:scanner:lint`).\n\n### Open questions for the human\n\n1. **Missing `baseline` file.**\n   - (a) Fail closed until a human commits one (an empty file means none).\n   - (b) Treat it as empty.\n   - (c) Ship an empty `baseline` in the starter.\n\n   **Recommend (a).** \"Beyond a committed baseline\" then always reflects a human decision, and `ard init` repos never get a surprise first run of 3×20 issues. The cost is a recorded failure every 24 h until the file exists, with a message naming the fix.\n2. **Linter scope for v1.**\n   - (a) Go via golangci-lint only.\n   - (b) Add shellcheck now (ard has shell scripts: `scan`, `regen.sh`, `deploy/*.sh`).\n   - (c) A pluggable SARIF-based design.\n\n   **Recommend (a)**, with (b) as the first follow-up issue. normalize.jq's candidate stage is the only part shellcheck would add to.\n3. **Report `//nolint` directives as findings?** (a) Yes (decision 8). (b) No, and rely on eng-review. **Recommend (a).** Without it, a worker can close a lint issue by suppressing it, and that counts towards Gate 3's \"merged with no human code edits\". It is about 30 lines of shell and jq.\n4. **Protect golangci-lint config.**\n   - Add `**/.golangci.{yml,yaml,toml,json}` to the starter's `protected_paths` (and ard's own, in the follow-up)? **Recommend yes.** Disabling a linter in config otherwise silently autocloses its issues. It only takes effect once the merger (#46 PR B) enforces protected paths.\n   - Keep the role-directory `golangci.yml` override? **Recommend yes**, as an optional human-owned file.\n5. **Collapsing identical messages in one file.**\n   - (a) Collapse into one finding.\n   - (b) Per-occurrence fingerprints with an index (`#2`), which renumber when an earlier one is fixed.\n   - (c) A count-aware baseline.\n\n   **Recommend (a) now and (c) as a follow-up if the gap shows up.** (b) churns fingerprints on unrelated fixes.\n6. **Severity table (decision 5).** Two levels, `medium` for bug-class rules and `low` for the rest. Confirm, or name rules to raise. It affects only filing order and suppression re-raise.\n\n### Done when\n\n- [ ] `scanners/lint/{scan,normalize.jq,Dockerfile}` are embedded, and `scan` is 0755 on disk and in `ard init`'s commit\n- [ ] Starter `config.yaml` has the lint override (plus the `.golangci.*` protected paths if open question 4 is accepted). `ard init`'s PR body has the baseline step\n- [ ] Golden, stubbed-scan, roles and initcmd tests pass with `make lint test`. `go test -tags integration ./internal/roles/` passes locally with golangci-lint and Docker\n- [ ] `make lint-scanner-fixtures` regenerates the real cases with no diff\n- [ ] Proposal (Scanners paragraph and table, `ard init` paragraph) and CLAUDE.md layout updated\n- [ ] Follow-up issues filed: shellcheck, toolchain switching, count-aware baseline, and the human `.ard/scanners/lint/` PR for ard itself\n\n### Resolved open questions (owner, 2026-11-23)\nThe owner accepted the plan's recommended answer for every open question above:\n1. Missing `baseline` file: fail closed until a human commits one; an empty file means none (option a).\n2. Linter scope for v1: Go via golangci-lint only; shellcheck is the first follow-up issue (option a).\n3. `//nolint` directives: reported as findings (decision 8).\n4. golangci-lint config: add `**/.golangci.{yml,yaml,toml,json}` to the starter's `protected_paths` (and ard's own in the follow-up), and keep the optional human-owned role-directory `golangci.yml` override.\n5. Identical messages in one file: collapse into one finding now; a count-aware baseline as a follow-up if the gap shows up (option a).\n6. Severity table: two levels, `medium` for bug-class rules and `low` for the rest, as in decision 5.\n\n","numLines":316,"startLine":1,"totalLines":316}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VmshbtRonkkKTis3zmQuyh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
