{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K2yiKgq1yWLnMoSGqxFfX9","type":"tool_result","content":"## Layout\n\n[docs/layout.md](docs/layout.md) lists every directory and package and what it holds. Read it to find where code lives; a PR that adds, removes or renames a directory or package updates that file, not this one.\n\nNew subcommands: implement the body in its own package as\n`func(ctx context.Context, e *cli.Env) error`, then add one field to\n`cli.Handlers` and one wiring line in `cmd/ard/main.go`'s `handlers()`.\nA nil handler runs the command as a \"not implemented yet\" stub.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nmake build   # bin/ard\nmake test    # go test ./...\nmake lint    # go vet + gofmt check\nmake fmt     # gofmt -w\n```\n\nRun `make lint test` before every commit.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Tests: table-driven, no network. Use the GitHub fake for unit tests; real-API tests go behind the `integration` build tag.\n- Errors: wrap with context (`fmt.Errorf(\"claim issue %d: %w\", n, err)`); never swallow.\n- Logging: structured (`log/slog`), one event per claim, close-out and failure.\n- Keep packages small and interfaces at the consumer.\n\n## Workflow\n\n- Work is tracked in GitHub issues with `phase:N`, `area:*` and `type:*` labels and a phase milestone. Pick from the lowest open phase.\n- Branch per issue: `<issue#>-<short-slug>`. Open a PR that says `Closes #<issue>`. Do not push to `main` directly.\n- Keep PRs to one issue. Note follow-ups as new issues rather than widening the PR.\n- Decision issues (`type:decision`) record the choice in a comment, then update the proposal and close.\nCLAUDE.md\ninternal/agent/claude/adapter.go\ninternal/agent/claude/adapter_test.go\ninternal/agent/claude/capture_test.go\ninternal/agent/claude/cli_integration_test.go\ninternal/agent/claude/cli_scripted_integration_test.go\ninternal/agent/claude/limit_parse_test.go\ninternal/agent/claude/parse.go\ninternal/agent/claude/parse_test.go\ninternal/agent/claude/prompt.go\ninternal/agent/claude/real_test.go\ninternal/agent/claude/scrub_test.go\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/CAPTURE.md\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_auth_bad_token.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_auth_bad_token.meta.json\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_auth_none.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_auth_none.meta.json\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_budget_exceeded.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_budget_exceeded.meta.json\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_error_max_turns.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_error_max_turns.meta.json\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_success.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_success.meta.json\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_agent_quotes_limit.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_api_retry_killed.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_api_retry_recovered.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_credits_required.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_limit_opus_text.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_limit_rejected_event.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_limit_resets_ms.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_limit_warning_only.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_throttle_not_usage_limit.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_truncated.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_usage.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_usage_limit.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_windows.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/windows_test.go","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5eb0b10-10f7-42ca-8b7a-846dd3a3e8b7","uuid":"221fdb8b-d687-4dc8-a19c-616c87cdf199","timestamp":"2026-11-23T21:28:20.889Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Layout\n\n[docs/layout.md](docs/layout.md) lists every directory and package and what it holds. Read it to find where code lives; a PR that adds, removes or renames a directory or package updates