{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLa14dGNXyE8PNP27QnA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A84hBJ3EAeudKw9XwWjdS3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef sub(p,a,b):\n    s=open(p).read(); assert a in s,(p,a); open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b,1))\nsub('docs/layout.md','scanners/error-codes, triage/lead','scanners/error-codes, scanners/lint, triage/lead')\nd='docs/proposal.md'\nsub(d,'| lint | repo linters, findings beyond a committed baseline |',\"| lint | golangci-lint per Go module (the repo's config, or the role's `golangci.yml`), plus `//nolint` directives, minus the role directory's `baseline` |\")\npara='''**The lint scanner** (`scanners/lint`, a `sh` script, one `jq` program and a Dockerfile that builds golangci-lint v2 with the image's Go) is Go only in v1; other ecosystems are follow-ups. It runs golangci-lint once per `go.mod` (pruning `.git`, `vendor`, `node_modules` and `testdata`) with the repo's own config, or a human-owned `golangci.yml` in the role directory when present. These flags are always forced after any config, because findings that vanish are autoclosed: `--max-issues-per-linter=0 --max-same-issues=0` (no truncation), `--new=false --new-from-rev= --new-from-merge-base= --new-from-patch=` (a repo config asking for \"new issues only\" would report nothing on a clean checkout), `--issues-exit-code=0 --fix=false --path-mode=abs`, plus JSON output to a temp file. It fails closed: a golangci-lint exit other than 0, a `typecheck` issue (a compile error), a module needing a newer Go than the image's (`GOTOOLCHAIN=local`; toolchain switching is a follow-up), a path outside the repository or with a control character, a malformed baseline, and a missing `baseline` file all exit non-zero with no output. Because the image builds golangci-lint with `CGO_ENABLED=0`, a repo config's `goplugin` custom linter cannot load and fails the run. The fingerprint is `lint:<rule>:<path>:<msg>`. `<rule>` is the linter plus `/<code>` for a check code (`staticcheck/SA4000`, `gosec/G104`), or for `govet` and `revive` an analyzer name (`govet/printf`). `<msg>` drops the code, control characters and repeated whitespace, and replaces every standalone number with `N`, so line numbers and \"complexity 31\" versus \"32\" never move a fingerprint; a fingerprint over 512 bytes has its message cut by runes. Identical fingerprints in one file collapse into one finding listing every line; the known gap is that a new occurrence of an identical message in the same file is hidden while the old one is open or baselined (a count-aware baseline is a follow-up). The group is `<rule>:<directory>`, so with `group_size: 20` issues are 20 per rule and directory. Severity has two levels: `medium` for `govet`, `staticcheck/SA*`, `gosec*`, `bodyclose`, `nilerr`, `nilnesserr`, `rowserrcheck`, `sqlclosecheck` and `durationcheck`, `low` for everything else; golangci-lint's own severity is ignored. Messages, source lines and paths are untrusted: they are rendered only inside `text` fences with ``` neutralised, and inline code spans have backticks replaced. Every `//nolint` directive in a `.go` file is itself a finding (rule `nolint`, group `nolint:<directory>`, `low`), so a worker cannot close a lint issue by suppressing it; for the same reason the starter protects `**/.golangci.{yml,yaml,toml,json}`. The baseline is the human-owned file `baseline` in the role directory (a protected path, so no agent can baseline a finding): `#` comments and blank lines are ignored, every other line is one fingerprint, and a finding whose fingerprint is listed is dropped. `ard init` does not ship one, so the scanner records a failure every 24 h until a human commits it; an empty file means no baseline. `scan --baseline` prints a baseline of all current findings (ignoring any existing one), and the exact Docker command is in the Dockerfile's header; the run logs how many baseline entries are unused. Baselining a finding that is open closes its issue as \"No longer detected\" (completed); to suppress it instead, close the issue as not planned. A golangci-lint version bump can change message text and so every fingerprint: bump the version and regenerate every repo's `baseline` in the same human PR.\n\n'''\ns=open(d).read()\ni=s.index('**The error-codes scanner**')\nopen(d,'w').write(s[:i]+para+s[i:])\nsub(d,'`.claude/` and `.mcp.json` (13 entries;','`.claude/` and `.mcp.json`, and the linter config a PR could weaken, `**/.golangci.yml`, `**/.golangci.yaml`, `**/.golangci.toml` and `**/.golangci.json` (17 entries;')\nsub(d,'CLAUDE.md, \"**/CLAUDE.md\", AGENTS.md, \"**/AGENTS.md\", .claude/, .mcp.json]','CLAUDE.md, \"**/CLAUDE.md\", AGENTS.md, \"**/AGENTS.md\", .claude/, .mcp.json, \"**/.golangci.yml\", \"**/.golangci.yaml\", \"**/.golangci.toml\", \"**/.golangci.json\"]')\nsub(d,'`scanners/error-codes`, `triage/lead`','`scanners/error-codes`, `scanners/lint`, `triage/lead`')\nsub(d,'the cve, docs, error-codes, lead,','the cve, docs, error-codes, lint, lead,')\nsub(d,'It also says to merge with **Squash and merge**','When the lint scanner is among the files, it also says the scanner fails until `.ard/scanners/lint/baseline` is committed. It also says to merge with **Squash and merge**')\nEOF\nsed -n 419,422p docs/proposal.md | cut -c1-120; git diff --stat | tail -3; go test ./internal/... 2>&1 | grep -v \"^ok\\|no test files\" | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":363,"cache_read_input_tokens":122933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":363},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5eb0b10-10f7-42ca-8b7a-8